          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>[An a]ccount of proceedings that took [place before u]s&mdash;we, the permanent court in Fus\u1e6d\u0101\u1e6d Egypt, appointed by his Excellency [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>[M]evorakh, Champion of Wisdom, Sage of the Academy, great Sanhed[rin, Prince] of Princes and Nagid of [Negidim &hellip; Lamp of]</li>\n<li>[the] West, Standard of the Sages, may his resting place be honor beneath the thro[ne of h]onor, and (appointed) by the mouth of his Excellency, Bea[uty of] Honor [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>and their glory, Prince of Princes and Nagid of the Negidim, and the strength of the entire house of Israel, &ldquo;Mordecai&rdquo; of the time, Standard of the Sage[s&hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip;] the Elder Ab\u016b al-Sur\u016br (our) tea(cher) and m(aster) Pera\u1e25ya, the beloved, (may his) Ro(ck) pr(eserve him) b. (his) h(onor,) g(reatness, and) h(oliness, our) tea(cher) and m(aster) Manasseh</li>\n<li>[&hellip;] the honored (who) r(ests) in E(den) came before the court, concerning the assets which were in his hand which he had employed in the trade of money-exchange. His mother, known as Nas[ab bt. &hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip;] our teacher and our master Joseph ha-Kohen the righteous, Head of the Court of all Israel, (may his) m(emory be) f(or a blessing), came (to the court), and she took upon herself [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip; and she wrote] a weighty agreement, a present debt concerning herself after she placed a pledge with him according to that document [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip;] upon him in accordance with his will, without condition upon it. The complete qinyan took place concerning tha[t&hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip; was] established in accordance with her will and preference. This interpretation and the rest of what it contains are upon him from beginning [to end &hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip; testimony] which was before us&mdash;we, the court, and whoever signs with us below&mdash;thus: [on &hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip;] to which we are accustomed, in Fus\u1e6d\u0101\u1e6d Egypt, situated on the Nile River, the Elder [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip; Ab\u016b] al-\u1e24asan (our) tea(cher) and m(aster) Eli the youth b. (our) tea(cher) and m(aster) Ma\u1e63lia\u1e25 the honored Elder (who) r(ests in) E(den,) and his mother, called Nas[ab &hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip;] our teacher [&hellip;] came to us &hellip; [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip;] &hellip; [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>[&hellip;] &hellip; [&hellip;]</li></ol>\n",
